  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Governmental funds from Exhibit D (trimmed p4), Total Governmental column. Transfers in = out = 655,534 (General 200,000 in / 355,534 out; Road 455,534 in; Inheritance Tax 300,000 out), cross-check ties. Beginning/ending cash are total governmental fund balances (3,151,122 / 3,069,638), which include Designated Investments of 158,460 (ending, Exhibit A p1/Exhibit C p3) plus pooled cash 2,911,178; investment fields left null because cash already includes them. Public Works mapped to streets/highways to tie to statement functions (includes General Fund noxious weed control 56,937). General Fund 'Taxes' line split using the General column of Exhibit D. Budget schedules give only totals per department (no object breakdown), so detail_category is not itemized. Nonmajor special revenue funds: 14 fund columns in Schedule 2, so the Total column is used; Schedule 3 per-fund budget schedule (pp12-14) shows only fund totals and is not recorded to avoid double counting. Exhibit D Road column differs in classification from Exhibit G (federal 13,936 vs 13,935, etc.) as printed; totals agree. No business-type funds; no balance sheet liabilities. Attempt 2 (targeted re-check): balance sheet now from Exhibit C, Balance Sheet - Cash Basis - Governmental Funds (p3, Total column, fund balance by classification: Restricted 526,804, Assigned 2,177,801, Unassigned 365,033), since its total 3,069,638 equals the government-wide Exhibit A (p1). Intergovernmental 1,032,832 has no printed breakdown by source, so it stays one state aid line. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
}
